Done. `addToCart` now takes an optional trailing `promoCode` parameter, and when it's truthy it's added to the cart request body as `promoCode` (sent on both the add and update paths); otherwise the field is absent and the request is unchanged.

```diff
-export const addToCart = (item, addToast, cartId, quantityCount, defaultStore, userData, selectedProductOptions) => {
+export const addToCart = (item, addToast, cartId, quantityCount, defaultStore, userData, selectedProductOptions, promoCode) => {
...
       }
+      if (promoCode) {
+        param.promoCode = promoCode;
+      }
       console.log('Cart parameters ' + JSON.stringify(param));
```

On the field name: the backend repo isn't in this workspace, so I inferred it from the backend's own cart response consumed here — [Cart.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/no_okf/work/g2_add_voucher/no_okf/codex/1/src/pages/other/Cart.js:416) reads `cartItems.promoCode`, which is the discount-code field the backend model exposes, so `promoCode` is the matching field in the cart-item request.

